--- body ---
## Context

Before running the full Experiment 1 sweep, design decisions must be explicitly
resolved and committed. Writing the Annex A spec first surfaced the open
questions. Pre-flight inspection of `experiments/prompts/modules/` revealed
that commit 4dc99e5 ("prompts: restructure modules to numbered scheme")
renamed every module file but did not propagate the rename into
`src/aedist/harness.py`, `modules/README.md`, or the sweep configs — so any
sweep launched today would crash on `base.txt` not found.

This ticket locks the design decisions and lands the harness fix in one
atomic change so the sweep is runnable end-to-end.

## Locked decisions

- **Assembly contract**: `2_goal.txt` and `5_table.txt` are implicitly always
  included (the post-rename equivalent of the old `base.txt`). Other modules
  are opt-in via `prompt_modules` in `experiments.toml`. The assembled prompt
  is the concatenation of selected modules **in filename lex order**, with
  the two always-modules slotted at their natural positions. No special
  prepend/append logic, no `_BEFORE_BASE` set.
- **Baseline prompt (Experiment 1)**: `prompt_modules = []` → just the
  always-pair (`2_goal` + `5_table`). No persona, no narratives, no quality
  bullets. The "Épouvantail" slide frame continues to display
  `prompt_extract.txt` as the strawman; the benchmark sweep uses the locked
  2_goal+5_table composition.
- **Model set**: `modelset_ablation_journal` v2 — 16 models × 5 repeats = 80 runs,
  organised around three language families (EN / FR / ZH) with multiple labs
  per family. All four SOTA Wave-2 agents (Opus 4.7, GPT-5.5, Mistral Large
  2512, Qwen 3 Max) are included so Experiment 2's "deep research vs
  parametric" claim can be tested within-model. Full IDs:
    EN — Anthropic: `anthropic/claude-opus-4.7`, `anthropic/claude-sonnet-4.6`, `anthropic/claude-haiku-4.5`
    EN — OpenAI:    `openai/gpt-5.5`, `openai/gpt-oss-120b`, `openai/gpt-oss-20b`
    FR — Mistral:   `mistralai/mistral-small-2603` (Small 4), `mistralai/mistral-medium-3.5`, `mistralai/mistral-large-2512` (Large 3)
    ZH — Qwen:      `qwen/qwen3.6-27b`, `qwen/qwen3.6-35b-a3b`, `qwen/qwen3.5-flash-02-23`, `qwen/qwen3.6-plus`, `qwen/qwen3-max`
    ZH — DeepSeek:  `deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro`, `deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash:free`
  No `-thinking` variants. `qwen/qwen3-max` (non-thinking) replaces the
  previous `qwen3-max-thinking`. Mistral version-numbers (Small 4 / Medium
  3.5 / Large 3) are per-tier branding by Mistral, not a generation order —
  noted in Annex A. The two `gpt-oss` models are MoE with configurable
  reasoning depth — for the parametric baseline, reasoning must be set to
  minimum/none (mirroring the no-thinking discipline for Qwen).
- **Sampling**: `temperature = 0.0`, `seed = 42`. Providers that ignore seed
  are documented in Annex A as a limitation, not a blocker.
- **System instruction (baseline)**: every API call carries a system message
  forbidding web search. Proposed exact text (revise in code review if
  needed):

      You have no web search capability. Do not claim to perform searches,
      do not invoke tools, do not fabricate URLs. Answer from parametric
      knowledge only.

  The instruction is sweep-scoped, not model-scoped — different regimes
  (RAG, livesearch) will use different system instructions in their own
  sweeps. Configured per-sweep via a new `system_instruction` field in
  `experiments.toml`.

## Actions

1. **Harness rename**: rewrite `src/aedist/harness.py::assemble_prompt`. Drop
   `_MODULE_ORDER`, `_BEFORE_BASE`, `base.txt`, and the persona-special-case.
   New contract: discover module files in `modules/`, always include
   `2_goal.txt` and `5_table.txt`, union with names listed in
   `prompt_modules`, sort the result lexicographically by filename, join with
   `"\n\n"`. `KNOWN_MODULES` becomes the set of files discovered at load.
   Validation rejects names that don't resolve to a file.

   Also: thread a `system_instruction: str | None` through the runner
   (`src/aedist/query_direct.py`). When non-empty, prepend
   `{"role": "system", "content": system_instruction}` to the messages list
   for both `query_single_turn` and `query_ollama_native` paths
   (currently lines 212/221). Surface it as a `system_instruction` field on
   sweep configs in `experiments.toml`. Baseline sweep value:
   `"You have no web search capability. Do not claim to perform searches, do not invoke tools, do not fabricate URLs. Answer from parametric knowledge only."`

2. **README**: rewrite `experiments/prompts/modules/README.md` to document
   the new scheme. Drop references to `base.txt` / `persona.txt` / etc.

3. **Tests**: fix `tests/test_modules_match_prompt_complete.py` (and any
   sibling that hardcodes old module names) so the suite passes.

4. **Sweep config**: update `experiments.toml`
   `[sweeps.sweep_ablation_p1_direct_base]`:
   - `prompt_modules = []`  (always-pair only)
   - `model_set = "modelset_ablation_journal"`
   - `repeat = 5`
   - `temperature = 0.0`, `seed = 42`
   Also audit and update the composite/RAG/livesearch sweeps so their
   `prompt_modules` lists use the new module names (e.g. `["1_persona",
   "3_overview", "4_narratives", "6_bibliography", "A_Statistics",
   "B_Temporality", "C_Uncertainty", "D_Completeness"]` — drop "2_goal" and
   "5_table" from any list since they are always-included).

5. **Model set rewrite**: replace `[sets.modelset_ablation_journal]` in
   `experiments.toml` with the 16-model v2 list (above). Add new entries to
   `experiments/models.yaml` for the 11 IDs not yet registered:
   `claude-opus-4.7`, `claude-haiku-4.5`, `gpt-5.5`, `gpt-oss-120b`,
   `gpt-oss-20b`, `mistral-medium-3.5`, `qwen3.6-27b`,
   `qwen3.5-flash-02-23`, `qwen3.6-plus`, `qwen3-max`, `deepseek-v4-pro`,
   `deepseek-v4-flash:free`. Each entry needs
   `name / route=openrouter / base_url / model_id / display_name / provider`.
   For `:free` suffix in `name`, verify the registry loader handles the colon
   (it's the OR-side variant separator). For both `gpt-oss-*`, configure the
   harness to request minimum reasoning depth (OpenAI's API parameter; check
   how OR exposes it — typically a `reasoning_effort` field or similar).

6. **Output directory cleanup**: `experiments/outputs/ablation/direct/p1_base/`
   currently holds 67 files from prior pilot + ticket-0057 extension runs
   (modelset_ablation_dev × 2 reps + census_extended set, pre-rename prompt
   semantics). Move to `experiments/outputs/ablation/direct/p1_base.pilot/`
   via `git mv` before 0177 launches, so `rebuild-measurements` does not
   mix pilot and journal data. Update `.gitignore` / data manifests if any
   reference the old path.

7. **Annex A**: update `slides/manuscript/main.md` Annex A to reference the
   `2_goal + 5_table` composition (not `base.txt`). Document which providers
   ignore `seed`.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] `harness.py` reads modules by filename-prefix order; no `base.txt` reference
- [ ] `modules/README.md` reflects the post-rename scheme
- [ ] `make check-fast` (or repo equivalent) passes — modules + assembly tests green
- [ ] `sweep_ablation_p1_direct_base` configured: `prompt_modules = []`, journal set, repeat=5, T=0, seed=42, budget_usd=10
- [ ] No retired model IDs in journal set
- [ ] `p1_base/` pilot files moved to `p1_base.pilot/` via `git mv`
- [ ] Annex A reflects locked decisions
- [ ] `make -C experiments preflight` passes (or repo equivalent) — assembled baseline prompt prints cleanly
